  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">R&#xe4;dda Barnen 2013-</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children 2013-</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children Sweden&#x2019;s (SCS) Child Right&#x2019;s Program addresses children&#x2019;s&#x2019; rights in terms of child right&#x2019;s governance, child protection and children&#x2019;s security in relation to HIV/Aids.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">R&#xe4;dda Barnens Child Rights Program syftar till att fr&#xe4;mja r&#xe4;ttigheter och m&#xf6;jligheter f&#xf6;r ett effektivt deltagande f&#xf6;r barn, och en &#xf6;kad medvetenhet om sina r&#xe4;ttigheter i linje med FN: s barnkonvention och ACRWC. Programmet fungerar i tre omr&#xe5;den n&#xe4;mligen barn r&#xe4;tt styrnings; skydd av barn; och barns s&#xe4;kerhet i f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llande till HIV / Aids.
Strategier som anv&#xe4;nds innefattar direkt programmering; kapacitetsuppbyggnad  av partner; gruppmedlemmar  och tull b&#xe4;rare; &#xf6;kad medvetenhet bland nyckelakt&#xf6;rer  som l&#xe4;rare, f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ldrar, traditionella ledare och mer; opinionsbildning f&#xf6;r att lobba p&#xe5; politikerna f&#xf6;r en barnv&#xe4;nlig lagstiftning och budget sp&#xe5;rning; barns deltagande f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att verksamheten speglar barnperspektivet ; och forskning och dokumentation f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;vervaka situationen f&#xf6;r barn och f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka medvetenheten om barns r&#xe4;ttigheter. Programmet &#xe4;r en del av SCI Zambia program som bygger p&#xe5; tidigare arbete inom samma geografiska platser.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children&apos;s Child Rights Program is aimed at promoting rights and possibilities for effective participation for children, and increased awareness of their rights in line with the UNCRC and the ACRWC. The program works in three areas namely child right&apos;s governance; child protection; and children&apos;s security in relation to HIV/Aids.
Strategies used include direct programming; capacity building of partners; community members and duty bearers; awareness raising among key stakeholders such as teachers, parents, traditional leaders and more;  advocacy to lobby on politicians for a child friendly legislative framework and budget tracking; child participation to ensure that the activities reflect the child perspective; and  research and documentation to monitor the situation of children and to raise the awareness of children&#x2019;s rights. The program is part of SCI Zambia program which builds on previous work in the same geographical locations.</narrative>
  </description>
